# jemdoc: menu{menu.jemdoc}{mathjax-test.html}, notime
= MathJax test page
Confirms that equations are rendered in your browser

This page exists so that you can check, with one click, that the mathematical typesetting of
the site works. If the three expressions below look like properly typeset mathematics, then
everything is fine. If you see raw dollar signs and backslashes instead, MathJax did not load
in your browser.

== 1. One inline equation

The received signal-to-noise ratio of user $k$ is $\gamma_k = p_k h_k / \sigma^2$, where
$p_k$ is the transmit power allocated to user $k$, $h_k$ is its channel gain, and $\sigma^2$
is the noise power.

== 2. One display equation

\(
\gamma_k = \frac{p_k\, h_k}{\sigma^2}, \qquad k = 1, 2, \ldots, K .
\)

== 3. Something slightly harder

\(
\begin{array}{ll}
\mbox{maximize} & \displaystyle \sum_{k=1}^{K} \log_2\!\left(1 + \gamma_k\right) \\
\mbox{subject to} & \displaystyle \sum_{k=1}^{K} p_k \le P_{\max}, \qquad p_k \ge 0 .
\end{array}
\)

== 4. If the equations do not appear

- MathJax is loaded from a public CDN, so a machine without internet access will show the raw
  LaTeX source. This is expected and harmless.
- Check that +www/mysite.conf+ still contains the +MathJax-script+ line.
- Check the browser console for a failed request to the MathJax URL.
- Remember that equations only work inside .jemdoc source files; they are rendered in the
  visitor's browser, not at build time.
